<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar outflows at $31.9 mln March 20.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar outflows at $31.9 mln March 20.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $31.9 million deficit on March 20 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>The Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON MARCH 20</p>
<p>Exports: $192.2 million</p>
<p>Imports: $259.2 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $253.6 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $218.5 million</p>
<p>Deficit: $31.9 million</p>
<p>MARCH DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $2.892 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $2.704 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $3.246 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $2.778 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $656 million ((-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 2485415))</p>
</text>
